            "explanation": "`iter_content` evaluates the built-in `type` callable when constructing an invalid-chunk-size `TypeError`. This indicates that the broader request utility code reports the runtime type of an invalid `chunk_size` value during validation. [Data: Entities (420); Relationships (1015)]\n\nThe `TYPE` entity is also described as being used for warning and error formatting in other contexts, including non-string passwords, unsupported header-part types, and fake-object construction in tests. Those uses are documented in the entity description, but no additional relationships are provided for them. [Data: Entities (420)]"
