    "title": "HTTP Digest Authentication and Hashing Utilities",
    "summary": "This community centers on `HTTPDigestAuth.build_digest_header`, a method that reads Digest authentication challenge fields and selects MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, or SHA-512 hashing helpers. The method defines nested UTF-8-aware digest functions and connects to string encoding, hexadecimal digest conversion, algorithm normalization, and challenge-field lookup operations. A separate test entity, `TEST_BINARY_PUT`, constructs a PUT request with encoded data and verifies that the request body is represented as bytes. The available data describes implementation relationships and test behavior, but does not provide evidence of legal compliance, organizational ownership, external reputation, misuse, or vulnerabilities.",
    "findings": [
        {
            "summary": "HTTP Digest authentication is the central capability",
