        {
            "summary": "The test community validates authenticated and TLS-enabled requests",
            "explanation": "The basic-authentication test expects authenticated GET requests to return status 200, unauthenticated requests to return status 401, and requests made after assigning session authentication to return status 200. This establishes explicit test coverage for session-level authentication behavior. [Data: Entities (1136, 1116); Relationships (1754)]\n\nThe session data also records assignment of a client certificate through `Session.cert`, and session GET calls using `verify=False` and a client certificate. These references show that TLS verification and client-certificate configuration are within the tested technical surface, while the available context does not provide a security assessment of those configurations. [Data: Entities (48, 1116); Relationships (40)]"
