            "summary": "Streaming responses and cleanup are explicitly tested",
            "explanation": "The community includes streamed session GET requests and a test that closes an unconsumed streamed response using `contextlib.closing`. That test asserts that response content remains unconsumed while the raw response is closed, indicating attention to connection and resource lifecycle behavior. [Data: Entities (1323, 1116, 1332); Relationships (2203, 2204)]\n\nThis is relevant to the technical importance of the community because session behavior extends beyond request dispatch to response consumption and cleanup. The evidence supports the existence of this lifecycle test but does not quantify resource usage, performance, or production impact."
